-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Running ATHENA from this tree
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This directory is the ATHENA runtime tree. It contains the Scheme programs,
packages, styles, tools, assets, and the executable under `bin/`.

For development builds, first build the executable from the repository root and
copy it here:

    cp -f build/src/ATHENA.bin ATHENA/bin/ATHENA.bin

Then run ATHENA from this directory:

    cd ATHENA
    ./StartATHENA.sh

The launcher currently uses the runtime settings that are known to work well on
the Linux Qt/xcb development setup:

    QT_QPA_PLATFORM=xcb
    QT_IM_MODULE=fcitx
    GTK_IM_MODULE=fcitx
    XMODIFIERS=@im=fcitx
    SDL_VIDEODRIVER=x11
    QT_FONT_DPI=180
    QT_AUTO_SCREEN_SCALE_FACTOR=0
    QT_SCALE_FACTOR=1
    QT_ENABLE_HIDPI_SCALING=1

It then starts:

    ./bin/ATHENA.bin --platform xcb

Any arguments passed to `StartATHENA.sh` are forwarded to `ATHENA.bin`.

For example:

    ./StartATHENA.sh --no-splash-screen
    ./StartATHENA.sh /path/to/document.ath

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Notes
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ATHENA is currently developed and tested on Linux with Qt. Legacy non-Qt GUI
backends have been removed from the maintained path, and this runtime setup has
not been tested on Windows or macOS.

If the program starts but input methods do not work, make sure fcitx is running
in your desktop session. If the interface scale is wrong, adjust `QT_FONT_DPI`
or `QT_SCALE_FACTOR` in `StartATHENA.sh`.
